RUN: not %COMPILE --error-format clang build plc.json 2>&1 | %CHECK %s

A call is rejected at any depth: inside the index of a source, and as the
condition of a jump. Text the parser cannot read in full is rejected too. Each
fault is located at the consuming element.
CHECK: {{.*}}unsupported_expression.cfc.unsupported_expression:1: error[E083]: Unsupported CFC expression: `arr[f()]`
CHECK: {{.*}}unsupported_expression.cfc.unsupported_expression:2: error[E083]: Unsupported CFC expression: `r + / 2`
CHECK: {{.*}}unsupported_expression.cfc.unsupported_expression:3: error[E083]: Unsupported CFC expression: `isReady()`
CHECK: error: Compilation aborted due to critical errors
